    <!-- Terms -->
    <!-- Acceptance screen text = summary of the Terms of Use (legal/en/terms.md) (document changes requiring re-acceptance → bump TERMS_VERSION). Key terms_placeholder_notice (historical name) is the intro sentence. -->
    <string name="terms_title">Before you start</string>
    <string name="terms_placeholder_notice">Domik is a free, unofficial, open source educational project (MIT licence) for controlling a 1st-generation Deimic controller on your home network.</string>
    <string name="terms_body">• This is not an official Deimic app or a replacement for it. The manufacturer is not affiliated with it, does not approve it and does not support it.\n\n• Your data stays with you. The author receives no data. The app controls your controller on your network, without any cloud. The Open-Meteo weather service receives only the place name you type and its approximate location.\n\n• Use at your own risk, without warranty. Bugs can happen, and the status on screen may differ from reality.\n\n• Don\'t rely on it for safety. Frost protection, pumps, heating and blinds must work without the app too. A command may not reach the controller, e.g. without a network or if the tablet switches off. Keep your wall switches and existing controls.\n\n• Only control your own installation – or someone else\'s with the owner\'s permission.\n\n• The serial number is the key to your home. Anyone who knows it and is on your network can control the installation. Never share it – including in reports on GitHub.\n\n• Download the app only from the official source: github.com/milwis/domik/releases.\n\nThis is a summary. The Terms of Use and Privacy Policy apply: github.com/milwis/domik/tree/main/legal. Your statutory consumer rights are not affected. Contact the author: github.com/milwis/domik/issues.\n\nTerms of Use version 1.0 of 10 October 2026. If you don\'t accept them, don\'t use the app.</string>
    <string name="terms_open_terms">Open the full Terms of Use</string>
